Wow!  Finally I win one, after many stupid deaths.  Strangely, it's
not quite my highest scoring game.  My highest score is still the one
where I walked into a moat and drowned on level 45.

Possible spoilers ahead.




Highlight: Threw Excalibur at a rust monster, who promptly ate it.  I
didn't realize rust monsters could eat rustproof goodies.  Guess I
won't do that again.  So I played the game with +5 Stormbringer.  It
worked.

The endgame is bizarre.  I can see how a ring of conflict would help.
Unfortuntely, I couldn't find one, in spite of a little polypiling.

Medusa was on level 25, castle level 29, and Wiz level 30.  I never
had to level teleport, as I walked through a trapdoor on the castle
level on purpose, looking for a level teleporter in Hell.  Checked my
mirror, and there he was.  Something else woke him up and he
immediately attacked me.  When I teleported to follow him, he turned
out to be sitting on the stairs up.  So I killed him, took the amulet,
and went right back up to the castle level.  It seemed very quick.
Then I just ran for my life.

At the end I was level 17, 225 HP, -34 AC, 702374 points.


